"fw : portland general electric : order rejecting tariff amendments ferc rejected the request by pge to modify the code of conduct so that they could buy on enrononline . basically , ferc did not believe that buying thru enrononline was a guarantee that consumers in oregon would not be harmed .
ferc found that there is , for
example , no assurance that the posted prices on enrononline
represent prevailing market prices .
applicants contend that , since pge can transact with epmi
