mssi awarded contract by the district of columbia to
provide it solutions to streamline current staffing requirements
capitol heights , maryland , april 21 , 2004 ( primezone ) - - management
solutions systems , inc . , ( otc bb : ijjp . ob ) a
wholly owned subsidiary of ijj corporation , a provider of it solutions to federal ,
state , and local government agencies , is pleased to announce that it was recently
awarded a contract by the district of columbia , department of human services ,
to develop an automated process to monitor and report vacant and staffed labor
positions . this application also tracks funding sources associated with each
position . the contract is expected to continue , based on a period of performance ,
until 2005 . ` ` this is a major milestone in furthering the objectives of
mssi in developing this web - enabled application to track departmental personnel
positions in the district of columbia , ' ' said mr . clifford pope , chief executive
officer of management solutions systems , inc . mr . pope also added that ,
` ` all dc agencies are required to report personnel information to the chief
financial officer ( cfo ) . currently , this reporting is performed annually at
the end of the fiscal year by submission of spreadsheets . therefore , the cfo ' s
office is only aware of real - time staffing information once a year . ' '
upon deployment of the schedule a online application , the three pilot agencies
will immediately be updating position information into a centralized database .
the cfo ' s office will then be able to view updated agency information in real - time .
the cfo will also be able to obtain information for statistical analysis and
trending reports at any time .
